0..73 Comment "// Equality derived from a data type\'s constructors (#2302): a definition"
74..145 Comment "// written `Eq.generic(T)` is structural equality over `T`, the checker"
146..217 Comment "// judging it as any declaration. Integers and strings compare by their"
218..297 Comment "// primitives, a sum by its side, a field of `T` itself recursively and a field"
298..364 Comment "// of another such type by that type\'s equality, written in place."
365..367 Comment "//"
368..445 Comment "// `Eq.generic.refl(T)` and `Eq.generic.sym(T)` prove that equality\'s laws by"
446..523 Comment "// congruence over `T`\'s constructors, resting on the laws the host admits of"
524..600 Comment "// integer and string equality, so a model of `Eq` whose members are derived"
601..678 Comment "// puts `T` under `==`. A field of a sum, as `Mark`\'s flag, or of `T` itself,"
679..757 Comment "// as `Peano`\'s, takes a proof the derivation does not write; the refusals are"
758..819 Comment "// beside `../../pathological/data/generic-eq-refused.gandr`."
